    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325-a1">

                <pb facs="0435" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg367"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor for the Department of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lansing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1915-04-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 2, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The enclosed memorandum
                    prepared six weeks ago you may think worthy of consideration in connection with
                    the letter I am sending you to-day regarding the death of Leon C. Thrasher
                    through the sinking of the British S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Falaba</hi> by
                    a German submarine.</p>
                <p>Since writing the memorandum I have been informed through different channels that
                    German public opinion takes a very similar view of the situation.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
